<title>JAPAN: Japan 1996 imported vehicle sales up 10.1% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan 1996 imported vehicle sales up 10.1% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Domestic sales of imported vehicles rose 10.1 percent in calendar 1996 from the previous year to a record 427,525 vehicles, the Japan Automobile Importers' Association (JAIA) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It was the fourth successive year of gains and surpassed the previous record of 388,162 vehicles marked last year.</p>
<p>Domestic sales of imported vehicles in December fell 2.1 percent from a year earlier to 38,059 vehicles, the first decline in four months on year-on-year basis.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of imported vehicle sales, with percentage changes from a year earlier:</p>
<p> Cars total		393,392 up   8.6 percent</p>
<p> - Cars over 2001 cc   277,769 up   7.9 percent</p>
<p> - Cars under 2000 cc  115,623 up  10.3 percent</p>
<p> Trucks total	    34,104  up  31.8 percent</p>
<p> Buses			   29  vs  13</p>
<p>Exporting countries and selected makers' car sales in Japan in 1996, with percentage changes from a year earlier:</p>
<p> German total		  184,133  up   17.9 percent</p>
<p>  Volkswagen Audi Group     60,306  up   31.5 percent</p>
<p>	     -Volkswagen	50,290  up   34.7 percent</p>
<p>	     -Audi		10,016  up   17.6 percent</p>
<p>	     Mercedes-Benz    40,975  up   16.5 percent</p>
<p>  Adam Opel		     38,339  up   18.0 percent</p>
<p>  BMW			     36,196  up    5.5 percent</p>
<p>  Ford-Werke AG		  6,296  down  1.9 percent</p>
<p>  Porsche			  1,900  up    2.9 percent</p>
<p> U.S. total		    122,559  down  0.3 percent</p>
<p>  Honda USA		     47,893  down  5.5 percent</p>
<p>  General Motors		22,101  up  140.6 percent</p>
<p>  Toyota			  20,152  down 38.7 percent</p>
<p>  Chrysler			16,170  up   11.5 percent</p>
<p>  Ford Motor		    14,713  up    2.0 percent</p>
<p> Britain total		  30,833  up    2.3 percent</p>
<p>  Rover group		   27,254  up    8.2 percent</p>
<p>  Jaguar			   2,686  up    0.5 percent</p>
<p> Sweden total		   24,938  up   14.1 percent</p>
<p>  Volvo			   24,037  up   17.2 percent</p>
<p>  Saab				 901  down 33.4 percent</p>
<p> Spain			     9,812  down 27.7 percent</p>
<p>  Nissan			   9,812  down 27.7 percent</p>
<p> Italy total		     7,059  up   33.9 percent</p>
<p>  Fiat group		     6,739  up   36.7 percent</p>
<p> Netherlands		     1,423  vs  nil</p>
<p>  Mitsubishi		     1,423  vs  nil</p>
<p> Australia			 1,436  down 38.1 percent</p>
<p>  Mitsubishi		     1,434  down 37.1 percent</p>
<p>General Motors' 1996 car sales included 11,467 GM-made Cavaliers sold by Toyota. The 1996 total included 8,569 Nissan AD vans made in Mexico, up 73.1 percent from the year before. The Australian total included two Nissan cars in 1996 against nil a year earlier.</p>
<p>Of the 1996 total, sales of vehicles produced by overseas units of Japanese makers totalled 90,682, down 15.1 percent from a year earlier.</p>
